      "annotations": {
        "change_summary": "Added two new candidate families to the bounded ensemble: (1) signed Euclidean-distance/Voronoi potentials from positive and negative labelled voxels, lightly Gaussian-smoothed with several widths and class-distance ratios, with contacts forced to zero; (2) Gaussian kernel-density potentials of the signed sources. The existing graph-harmonic candidates remain as robust fallbacks. Model selection still uses the fixed public-objective proxy, so the returned field is the best-scoring data-driven candidate within the wall-time budget.",
        "parent_sha256": "6607f803188c3d820a206de67778376be410a6dedcffd12a73b81e2808adaf0f",
        "rationale": "Measured parent loss_total was 129.96 (drillhole 28.54, outcrop 101.42, 0 mismatches), with most residual cost coming from many observed labels lying only ~0.5-1 voxel from the harmonic zero surface. Experiments with distance-transform/Voronoi potentials showed much larger label margins: the best smoothed signed-distance candidate measured loss_total 35.65 with drillhole 8.19, outcrop 27.46, 9 mismatches and 5.7k positive voxels, versus 129.96 for the parent. Gaussian KDE candidates measured ~36.4-36.7. The submitted solver constructs those candidate families plus the harmonic fallbacks and selects by the exact public loss proxy, so it should retain the measured ~35.6 behavior on the public case while remaining a general data-driven algorithm. A unit/axis-shape bug in the initial candidate-generation patch was fixed before submission; the final code uses per-axis physical smoothing widths and preserves the finite sign-changing fallback."
