        "rationale": "Measured parent was loss_total 35.645 (drillhole 8.187, outcrop 27.458, 9 mismatches). Diagnostics showed the remaining gap was dominated by ~510 observed labels at distance 1-2 from contacts/opposite labels, where the smooth separating surface sat closer than necessary (~0.84 actual vs ~1.0 bound). A measured local-bump candidate improved to 35.606. The submitted solver adds a bounded family of such corrections and selects by the exact objective proxy. Public selfcheck passes; the measured public-case result is now loss_total 35.599 (drillhole 8.118, outcrop 27.481, 9 mismatches, 5727 positive voxels) in 3.8 s, slightly better than the parent. The gain is modest because the remaining cost is largely geometric: many labels have bound distances of only 1-2 voxels due to adjacent contacts/opposite labels."
